# Inverted gitignore: deny everything, then re-include the workspace layer.
#
# Inner repositories checked out into this workspace are swallowed by the
# deny-all rule below. Git never descends into them, so they produce no gitlink
# even under `git add -A`.
#
# A directory must be un-ignored TWICE: the directory itself (so git descends
# into it) and its contents (so files inside are tracked).

*

# Workspace layer — files
!.gitignore
!.seedignore
!.editorconfig
!AGENTS.md
!CHANGELOG.md
!CLAUDE.md
!CONTRACT.md
!README.md
!dprint.json
!garden.yaml
!workspace.toml

# Template-repository-only files: listed in .seedignore, so they never reach
# a workspace created from this template.
!CONTRIBUTING.md
!LICENSE-APACHE
!LICENSE-MIT

# Workspace layer — directories
!.github/
!.github/**
!.githooks/
!.githooks/**
!.claude/
!.claude/**
!.agents/
!.agents/**
!.skills/
!.skills/**
!bin/
!bin/**
!context/
!context/**

# Machine-generated garden trees, derived wholesale from workspace.toml by
# `aw bootstrap`. Never tracked — the manifest is the single source of truth.
.aw/

# Scratch directory: tracked as an empty marker only.
!tmp/
tmp/**
!tmp/.keep

# Hard exclusions — last match wins. Whole directories are re-included above,
# so anything a tool drops inside one is tracked unless named here.

# Secrets.
*.env

# Operating-system droppings.
.DS_Store
._*
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Editor scratch.
*~
*.swp
.#*

# Merge and patch residue.
*.orig
*.rej
